  "worked_solution": "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{3}{4}{t}^{3}-6t+1),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{5}{{t}^{3}})\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{9}{4}{t}^{2}-6,\\frac{15}{{t}^{4}}\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
